	\item $\rmsg{x}{Y}{}, \rmsg{x}{Z}{}$: as the protocol is deterministic, and the input of $x$ is independent of the value of $\rid{-y_i}$, the messages are independent of the event also. 
	\item $\ridlayer{X}, \ensuremath{\bm{\mathcal{J}}_{\textnormal{all}}}, \ensuremath{\bm{L}_{\textnormal{all}}}$ and $\ensuremath{\bm{\mathcal{K}}_{\textnormal{all}}}$ barring $\rcKupdown{x \to Y}{t, i}$: all these sets are disjoint from sets in collection $\ensuremath{\mathcal{K}}$, and therefore are independent of what happens inside $\ensuremath{\mathcal{K}}$. 
